## Conversation
Part of the Kimi-K3 GB300 bring-up. The K3 matrix entry needed FlashInfer
v0.6.15.post1 to SKIP the v0.6.14 patch; the original APPLY_FLASHINFER_PATCH
boolean was added for that, then deleted in favor of this mechanism once a
second, version-specific patch (SITU) appeared.

## Actions
Moved flashinfer-v0.6.14-deepseekv3-no-group-routing.patch under
flashinfer-patches/v0.6.14/, rewrote the Dockerfile patch step as a find|xargs
sweep over flashinfer-patches/${FLASHINFER_COMMIT}, deleted the
APPLY_FLASHINFER_PATCH build-arg from the workflow and the
apply-flashinfer-patch key from the matrix config.

## Errors & Mistakes
None in this commit; the predecessor boolean shipped in 38e0487 and its
"skip only on explicit 0" semantics existed because the workflow renders an
empty build-arg for matrix entries that omit the key.

## Dead Ends
The boolean toggle itself: two live configs did genuinely differ, but the
version already encodes which patches apply, so the knob was redundant.

## Hints for Future Agents
A FlashInfer version with no flashinfer-patches/<version>/ directory gets no
patches — that is intentional, not an omission. Patch file names inside a
version dir sort lexically; number them if order ever matters.

## Codebase Discoveries
git -C flashinfer apply runs in the flashinfer-downloader stage, so patched
SOURCE feeds flashinfer-builder; nothing patches installed wheels.

